(ns amu.granted-region-dequant
  (:export [dot-q8-0]))

;; granted regions x dequant: the fused dequantize-and-dot over TWO regions the
;; caller granted -- a packed weight row and the activations it folds against.
;;
;; Five parameters is the whole ABI budget, and it is exactly what this takes:
;; two words per region and the block count. Both bases are parameters, so the
;; provenance rule admits them and `kotoba.verifier`'s own re-derivation agrees;
;; the program never names an address.
;;
;; The point of the fixture is CROSS-ISA AGREEMENT. `kernel-dequant-dot-q8-0`'s
;; contract is an accumulation tree, not a dot product -- floating-point
;; addition is not associative, so one order of summation IS the operation --
;; and the AArch64 arm exists only because it reproduces the x86 one. The test
;; beside this file asserts the two answers are equal TO EACH OTHER, not merely
;; that each equals a constant: a constant both arms had drifted from together
;; would still pass the weaker claim.

(defn dot-q8-0 [wbase :i64 wlen :i64 xbase :i64 xlen :i64 blocks :i64]
  (kernel-dequant-dot-q8-0 wbase wlen xbase xlen blocks))
